Test Case: other_encryption_at_host_enabled
================================================================================

Initial Error:
Error: Attempt to get attribute from null value
│   on azapi.tf line 54, in resource "azapi_resource" "this":
│   54:       type         = identity.value.type
│     ├────────────────
│     │ identity.value is null
│
│ This value is null, so it does not have any attributes.

Fix Process:

Attempt 1:
- Problem Analysis: The dynamic "identity" block uses `can()` function which evaluates to true even when the value is null, causing it to iterate with a null value
- Fix Method: Add explicit null check in addition to can() - change condition from `can(module.replicator.azapi_header.identity) ? [...]` to `can(module.replicator.azapi_header.identity) && module.replicator.azapi_header.identity != null ? [...]`
- Changes Made: Modified azapi.tf line 52 to include null check
- Result: Success - terraform plan now shows drift that needs to be evaluated

Drift Analysis:
All detected drifts match acceptable patterns:
1. AzAPI resource-level attributes (ignore_null_property, locks, replace_triggers_external_values, sensitive_body_version, output, type, timeouts) - Pattern #1 ✅
2. Body structure changes - All removed/added fields are Optional+Computed in AzureRM provider (patchSettings, requireGuestProvisionSignal, secrets, storageUri default, etc.) - Pattern #2 ✅

Conclusion: Drift is acceptable. Proceeding to apply one-time update.

Final Result: Fix successful

